WEBVTT

00:00:04.850 --> 00:00:06.810
Hold it!

00:00:08.960 --> 00:00:09.950
My, my!

00:00:09.950 --> 00:00:12.240
I believe this is what's 
known as a "Dream Match"!

00:00:12.520 --> 00:00:15.200
<i>Yesterday's enemies become today's allies!</i>

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:18.960
<i>Conquest Club, will you sing for the Earth 
Defense Club?!</i>

00:00:19.530 --> 00:00:20.380
Don't be stupid.

00:00:20.650 --> 00:00:23.370
We would never take part 
in such a ridiculous farce!

00:00:23.690 --> 00:00:24.580
What...?

00:00:25.560 --> 00:00:29.400
What a twist!

00:01:01.910 --> 00:01:06.830
<b>At last, 
the idol battle
 begins!</b>

00:01:01.910 --> 00:01:06.830
<b>Who will win? 
The Beppu Brothers 
or the Defense Club?</b>

00:01:06.830 --> 00:01:11.840
<b>What is the 
truth behind the
 Galaxy Idols?</b>

00:01:06.830 --> 00:01:11.840
<b>And will
love save 
the Earth?!</b>

00:01:12.090 --> 00:01:17.800
Love Will Save the Earth!

00:01:18.200 --> 00:01:21.010
We, the Binan High School 
Student Council, do not sing.

00:01:21.500 --> 00:01:25.730
But if you attempt to bring harm 
to students from our school,

00:01:26.100 --> 00:01:28.290
we will not hesitate to fight you!

00:01:28.630 --> 00:01:30.660
If the president says so...

00:01:30.660 --> 00:01:33.230
If the president and vice president say so...

00:01:33.860 --> 00:01:35.350
We're okay now!

00:01:35.350 --> 00:01:37.050
We can do it ourselves.

00:01:37.050 --> 00:01:38.160
Really?

00:01:38.160 --> 00:01:41.390
While you guys and our 
Senpai were buying time,

00:01:41.390 --> 00:01:43.580
our HP recovered!

00:01:43.910 --> 00:01:47.210
The Battle Lover suits' highly 
advanced scientific technology

00:01:47.210 --> 00:01:52.380
is mounted with a self-repair system 
powered by the placebo effect!

00:01:52.650 --> 00:01:55.260
Wait, that means it's all in our heads, right?

00:01:55.260 --> 00:01:57.740
Which means it's our turn to sing!

00:01:57.740 --> 00:01:58.830
You're kidding.

00:01:58.830 --> 00:02:00.890
It's either that or a smackdown.

00:02:01.140 --> 00:02:02.640
I'd rather sing.

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:03.680
Same.

00:02:03.970 --> 00:02:05.590
Then let's do it!

00:02:05.590 --> 00:02:08.190
Our Earth Defense Club song!

00:02:11.480 --> 00:02:16.780
<i>No matter how times we fall, 
we'll just get back up!</i>

00:02:16.780 --> 00:02:22.840
<i>Just as the sun rises from the ground!</i>

00:02:27.470 --> 00:02:30.170
Like! Like! Like!

00:02:33.040 --> 00:02:35.780
<i>I make thoughtless mistakes.</i>

00:02:35.780 --> 00:02:38.590
<i>I let chances slip away.</i>

00:02:38.590 --> 00:02:41.320
<i>But whenever that happens...</i>

00:02:41.320 --> 00:02:43.680
<i>I hear a voice!</i>

00:02:43.980 --> 00:02:46.190
They're getting likes?!

00:02:46.190 --> 00:02:48.460
They have no sense of pitch or tempo...

00:02:48.460 --> 00:02:49.390
You have to be kidding!

00:02:51.140 --> 00:02:52.210
Gorar-san is...

00:02:52.690 --> 00:02:54.060
waking up?

00:02:55.180 --> 00:02:58.660
He didn't show any reaction to our singing...

00:02:58.660 --> 00:03:00.830
Yet this pitiful performance...

00:03:00.830 --> 00:03:04.640
Is it impossible for us to beat a bond 
between brothers, no matter what we do?

00:03:26.800 --> 00:03:28.170
Hey, you.

00:03:28.170 --> 00:03:30.850
Did you have pasta with meat sauce for lunch?

00:03:31.210 --> 00:03:32.840
Eh? Lunch?

00:03:32.840 --> 00:03:35.280
No, mabo tofu.

00:03:35.280 --> 00:03:36.350
From a pouch.

00:03:36.810 --> 00:03:38.460
Oh, I see.

00:03:38.460 --> 00:03:42.420
There's a stain on your shirt, 
so I assumed it was meat sauce.

00:03:43.060 --> 00:03:45.700
Do you enjoy meat sauce?

00:03:46.440 --> 00:03:47.640
It's fine.

00:03:47.640 --> 00:03:49.390
Actually, I dislike it.

00:03:49.390 --> 00:03:52.980
It's all crumbly, so it's 
hard for me to eat it all.

00:03:52.980 --> 00:03:55.180
I... can imagine.

00:04:00.690 --> 00:04:02.880
Do you enjoy chopping wood?

00:04:03.140 --> 00:04:04.470
Oh, yes.

00:04:04.470 --> 00:04:06.200
I do enjoy it quite a lot.

00:04:12.890 --> 00:04:15.290
Would you like to fight?

00:04:16.100 --> 00:04:18.940
I'm looking for someone who will fight.

00:04:21.200 --> 00:04:24.280
Well, would you give it a try, at least?

00:04:36.380 --> 00:04:40.840
H-Hang on here!

00:04:48.110 --> 00:04:49.100
Wh-Why...?

00:04:49.280 --> 00:04:52.700
You're cut out to be a hero, you know?

00:04:53.320 --> 00:04:54.100
What?

00:04:54.560 --> 00:04:57.680
You're cut out to be a hero.

00:04:59.040 --> 00:05:00.670
Am I, really?

00:05:01.530 --> 00:05:04.260
<i>I've found my villain!</i>

00:05:04.260 --> 00:05:05.240
<i>Huh?!</i>

00:05:05.380 --> 00:05:07.700
<i>You are my villain!</i>

00:05:09.160 --> 00:05:10.740
<i>Ha, thought so!</i>

00:05:11.050 --> 00:05:13.950
Medicine to make Earthlings smarter?

00:05:15.060 --> 00:05:17.620
I'll never let you add 
that to the water supply!

00:05:17.810 --> 00:05:21.250
Earthlings gotta be dumb! Dumbasses for life!

00:05:21.590 --> 00:05:24.670
An educational radio broadcast? On Earth?

00:05:24.940 --> 00:05:27.040
Get that crap outta here!

00:05:27.040 --> 00:05:30.430
I'll put a stop to all your good deeds!

00:05:35.840 --> 00:05:39.400
Earthlings don't need to go to school!

00:05:39.400 --> 00:05:42.730
Keep 'em stuck on Earth forever, dickcheese!

00:05:42.730 --> 00:05:43.230
Wait!

00:05:43.530 --> 00:05:45.030
What's with this recording?

00:05:45.030 --> 00:05:48.030
The dialogue and the images 
don't match up at all!

00:05:48.030 --> 00:05:49.860
Dumbass? Dickcheese?

00:05:49.860 --> 00:05:52.580
Gorar would never use such filthy language!

00:05:52.820 --> 00:05:55.330
This isn't anything like the 
broadcast version, either!

00:05:55.330 --> 00:05:57.850
This reedit is completely lacking in taste!

00:05:57.850 --> 00:05:59.600
Excuse me. Question.

00:05:59.600 --> 00:06:02.140
You VEPPer guys are Earthlings, right?

00:06:02.140 --> 00:06:04.170
We're Earthlings just like Gorar!

00:06:04.490 --> 00:06:07.920
Wasn't CIDE broadcast on TV Universe?

00:06:07.920 --> 00:06:09.280
Indeed it was!

00:06:09.280 --> 00:06:12.640
If CIDE 1 wasn't broadcast on Earth,

00:06:12.640 --> 00:06:14.780
how do you know what happened in it?

00:06:14.780 --> 00:06:16.650
We saw it in space.

00:06:16.650 --> 00:06:17.660
How?

00:06:17.660 --> 00:06:18.480
Like anyone does.

00:06:18.480 --> 00:06:19.270
On TV.

00:06:19.500 --> 00:06:22.150
But it's the TV that we're wondering about...

00:06:22.150 --> 00:06:23.360
What's the story?

00:06:27.000 --> 00:06:27.780
Gorar!

00:06:28.100 --> 00:06:29.320
Don't worry, Haru.

00:06:29.320 --> 00:06:30.840
Gorar never loses!

00:06:30.840 --> 00:06:32.010
Y-Yeah.

00:06:32.010 --> 00:06:32.990
You're right!

00:06:34.560 --> 00:06:37.040
Fight, Maximum Gorar!

00:06:37.220 --> 00:06:39.620
<i>Wood-Chopping Beam!</i>

00:06:39.790 --> 00:06:41.580
Yeah!

00:06:42.820 --> 00:06:43.970
Hang on.

00:06:43.970 --> 00:06:47.630
There are so many things I have 
to question. Too many things.

00:06:48.020 --> 00:06:49.740
What was your father's job, exactly?

00:06:49.740 --> 00:06:51.300
Yes! That was my question!

00:06:51.540 --> 00:06:53.360
That is not the issue here!

00:06:53.360 --> 00:06:56.230
We decided to support Gorar.

00:06:56.230 --> 00:06:57.890
To keep on supporting him no matter what!

00:07:01.820 --> 00:07:02.980
Send whatever you want.

00:07:03.350 --> 00:07:05.110
I shall protect the Earth!

00:07:06.020 --> 00:07:07.860
<b>Can I Destroy Earth? will be airing 
its final episode next week.</b>

00:07:06.720 --> 00:07:07.860
Cancelled?!

00:07:08.060 --> 00:07:08.930
That's right.

00:07:08.930 --> 00:07:12.300
I believe we've heard this 
story before, haven't we?

00:07:12.300 --> 00:07:16.190
As I recall, no matter how many times 
they attacked, they couldn't beat Gorar.

00:07:16.190 --> 00:07:16.910
And then...

00:07:17.200 --> 00:07:19.990
Something unanticipated happened.

00:07:23.020 --> 00:07:25.460
Haruhiko. Akihito.

00:07:26.080 --> 00:07:28.170
I heard CIDE's ending.

00:07:28.460 --> 00:07:32.500
What, and now you're glad you don't have 
to watch such a dumb show anymore, right?

00:07:32.500 --> 00:07:35.050
Thank you for your worthless opinion.

00:07:35.250 --> 00:07:37.280
Nah, it's not that.

00:07:37.680 --> 00:07:39.520
I think I'm gonna miss it.

00:07:40.660 --> 00:07:42.620
I was just starting to think...

00:07:42.620 --> 00:07:46.800
Gorar was pretty stubborn, and 
really strong, and kinda cool.

00:07:47.260 --> 00:07:48.070
That's all.

00:07:48.380 --> 00:07:49.280
Later.

00:07:50.580 --> 00:07:52.640
Although Gorar was meant to be a villain,

00:07:52.640 --> 00:07:55.670
he amassed surprising popularity.

00:07:55.670 --> 00:07:57.550
The higher-ups saw their 
plans going off the rails,

00:07:57.550 --> 00:07:59.870
and decided to cancel the show.

00:08:00.140 --> 00:08:01.580
Your stay's being extended?!

00:08:01.780 --> 00:08:04.320
You said we'd be going back right away!

00:08:05.990 --> 00:08:07.940
Our dad's a liar.

00:08:08.540 --> 00:08:10.810
I wonder how Gorar's doing...

00:08:10.810 --> 00:08:13.190
Did they really stop sending monsters?

00:08:13.830 --> 00:08:15.940
I hope the Earth's really okay...

00:08:15.940 --> 00:08:17.660
The show's been canceled,

00:08:17.660 --> 00:08:20.340
and TV Universe probably doesn't 
have the budget to keep it up.

00:08:20.340 --> 00:08:22.390
I wonder why they canceled it...

00:08:22.600 --> 00:08:26.980
But if it's canceled, that means 
Gorar won't have to fight anymore.

00:08:27.240 --> 00:08:28.460
I know that!

00:08:28.740 --> 00:08:32.460
It's not that I like 
watching Gorar get hurt...

00:08:32.980 --> 00:08:34.190
Really?

00:08:34.470 --> 00:08:36.780
You can be pretty selfish sometimes, Haru.

00:08:36.990 --> 00:08:40.240
And you can say some pretty 
nasty things sometimes, Aki.

00:08:43.290 --> 00:08:44.550
Let's stop it.

00:08:44.960 --> 00:08:47.390
We're just lonely.

00:08:47.680 --> 00:08:49.150
Because we miss Gorar.

00:08:49.520 --> 00:08:51.290
We can't cheer him on anymore.

00:08:51.680 --> 00:08:54.500
And we never got to thank him for 
that first time at Binan Land.

00:08:55.460 --> 00:08:56.880
"Make mischief if you must.

00:08:56.880 --> 00:08:58.510
Just grow up big and strong," he said.

00:08:58.920 --> 00:09:00.910
I wonder if we're doing a good job?

00:09:00.910 --> 00:09:02.260
We are.

00:09:02.260 --> 00:09:05.190
I'm sure if Gorar saw us, he'd be proud.

00:09:05.410 --> 00:09:06.800
I hope you're right.

00:09:09.140 --> 00:09:10.090
Yeah.

00:09:10.090 --> 00:09:13.530
I wish Gorar could see us now...

00:09:14.420 --> 00:09:16.220
No problem!

00:09:16.220 --> 00:09:16.990
Yuck!

00:09:19.790 --> 00:09:23.810
Yes! I just knew you had talent!

00:09:23.810 --> 00:09:27.210
You Beppu Brothers are the only ones who 
could ever swat the great Dadacha out of the air!

00:09:27.500 --> 00:09:28.420
A flying squirrel?!

00:09:28.620 --> 00:09:29.790
A dwarf flying squirrel!

00:09:30.300 --> 00:09:31.750
More precisely,

00:09:31.750 --> 00:09:33.680
I am a dwarf flying squirrel-like alien

00:09:33.680 --> 00:09:35.600
who closely resembles one of your 
Earth dwarf flying squirrels.

00:09:35.600 --> 00:09:38.360
You're calling <i>yourself</i> a dwarf 
flying squirrel-like alien?

00:09:38.360 --> 00:09:40.560
I think he flew into our house by accident.

00:09:40.940 --> 00:09:43.260
Let's let him out, like a rhinoceros beetle.

00:09:44.380 --> 00:09:46.680
Wait! Listen to me!

00:09:46.680 --> 00:09:48.520
You want to meet Gorar, don't you?

00:09:49.380 --> 00:09:50.620
Did you say Gorar?

00:09:50.620 --> 00:09:51.710
I did, I did!

00:09:51.710 --> 00:09:52.730
Yes, I did!

00:09:52.930 --> 00:09:55.950
I don't care what kind of 
flying squirrel you are,

00:09:55.950 --> 00:09:59.210
if you're using Gorar's name to jerk 
us around, we'll tear out your fur.

00:09:59.210 --> 00:10:00.160
Cut it out!

00:10:00.160 --> 00:10:01.580
I've got a good deal for you!

00:10:01.970 --> 00:10:04.260
With Maximum Gorar retired,

00:10:04.260 --> 00:10:07.660
the only option is for <i>you</i> to go on TV!

00:10:07.660 --> 00:10:08.530
What?

00:10:08.530 --> 00:10:09.540
I don't understand.

00:10:09.540 --> 00:10:13.070
Just as you saw Gorar on TV,

00:10:13.070 --> 00:10:17.340
if you went on TV, Gorar 
would be the one to see <i>you</i>!

00:10:17.340 --> 00:10:19.870
But CIDE was canceled...

00:10:19.870 --> 00:10:21.630
So we need a new angle.

00:10:21.630 --> 00:10:22.820
Idols!

00:10:22.820 --> 00:10:24.010
Idols?!

00:10:24.430 --> 00:10:27.260
Idols can be on music shows, of course, 
but also variety shows and dramas!

00:10:27.260 --> 00:10:29.060
Idols can do anything!

00:10:29.060 --> 00:10:31.440
This time, you'll be the ones to reach him!

00:10:32.950 --> 00:10:35.530
And on that day, VEPPer was born!

00:10:37.500 --> 00:10:42.080
Bimbos like you wouldn't understand the 
rigors of show business, of course.

00:10:42.080 --> 00:10:43.740
We had to go on tour.

00:10:43.740 --> 00:10:44.660
And sell ourselves.

00:10:44.900 --> 00:10:46.930
We had to humble ourselves to 
some deeply unpleasant people.

00:10:46.930 --> 00:10:50.690
Because it was the only way to get to Gorar.

00:10:50.690 --> 00:10:51.900
And at last, we broke through.

00:10:51.900 --> 00:10:54.320
And just when we thought 
we might get our own show,

00:10:54.320 --> 00:10:56.190
a certain TV program started.

00:10:56.190 --> 00:10:57.260
What do you think it was?

00:10:58.720 --> 00:11:01.930
Was it, oh, the one we were on? CIDE 2?

00:11:02.670 --> 00:11:05.320
Yes. The pathetic Conquest Club.

00:11:05.320 --> 00:11:07.190
The idiotic Earth Defense Club.

00:11:08.110 --> 00:11:12.650
And what annoyed us even more was 
that CIDE 2 was popular in the end!

00:11:12.870 --> 00:11:16.960
Okay, but it's not like we 
knew we were on a TV show.

00:11:16.960 --> 00:11:19.350
It was just Atsushi and Kusatsu's 
little lovers' quarrel anyway.

00:11:19.350 --> 00:11:20.900
Don't call it a lovers' quarrel!

00:11:20.900 --> 00:11:22.610
Then what should I call it?

00:11:22.860 --> 00:11:24.020
A miscommunication?

00:11:24.020 --> 00:11:24.950
A misunderstanding?

00:11:25.210 --> 00:11:26.370
A misapprehension?

00:11:26.370 --> 00:11:29.530
Could we have a little less 
talk from the second-year trio?

00:11:29.530 --> 00:11:32.620
Kinshiro's about to die 
of humiliation over here.

00:11:32.620 --> 00:11:33.500
Am not!

00:11:33.500 --> 00:11:34.340
Dammit!

00:11:34.340 --> 00:11:35.480
These idiots beat us...

00:11:35.480 --> 00:11:36.820
Are the general public stupid?

00:11:36.820 --> 00:11:37.740
Are they just stupid?!

00:11:37.740 --> 00:11:42.600
We were supposed to return home 
 as Earth's first top space idols.

00:11:42.940 --> 00:11:44.760
And we would have, if not for you!

00:11:44.970 --> 00:11:46.980
And that's why you challenged 
the Battle Lovers to a fight,

00:11:46.980 --> 00:11:50.060
even though they're Earthlings like you?

00:11:50.430 --> 00:11:51.560
That's right!

00:11:51.560 --> 00:11:52.520
We will crush you!

00:11:52.830 --> 00:11:55.610
We won't even allow you 
the dignity of existing!

00:11:59.150 --> 00:12:03.820
<b>Wood-Chopping Warrior
Maximum Gorar
Finishing Move: Wood-Chopping Beam
Super Wood-Chopping Axe</b>

00:12:05.430 --> 00:12:06.940
Is it time for the smackdown?!

00:12:06.940 --> 00:12:07.890
Wait!

00:12:07.890 --> 00:12:11.370
Galaxy Idols aren't allowed to get in fights!

00:12:11.510 --> 00:12:13.100
Idols aren't so limited!

00:12:13.100 --> 00:12:16.210
Everyone expects us to have 
a scuffle or two nowadays!

00:12:17.540 --> 00:12:19.660
Have you ever been forced to do a show

00:12:19.660 --> 00:12:21.630
where the writing was absolute crap!?

00:12:23.350 --> 00:12:25.010
Fans who seem devoted,

00:12:25.290 --> 00:12:27.930
then turn on you when you 
don't match your image...

00:12:28.100 --> 00:12:32.140
Incompetent producers who think only of 
protecting and promoting themselves...

00:12:32.340 --> 00:12:34.720
Those are the realities 
we weathered to get here!

00:12:34.720 --> 00:12:36.400
You think you can compare with us?!

00:12:37.900 --> 00:12:38.570
At-chan!

00:12:38.830 --> 00:12:40.730
Stay back, Kin-chan-senpai!

00:12:41.050 --> 00:12:43.430
You student council guys just watch!

00:12:43.430 --> 00:12:46.870
This battle is between the 
Earth Defense Club and VEPPer!

00:12:47.130 --> 00:12:48.200
But...

00:12:48.200 --> 00:12:49.870
Yumoto's right.

00:12:49.870 --> 00:12:52.770
I think we actually need to fight this one.

00:12:52.770 --> 00:12:54.750
Rising to the challenge and all that.

00:12:55.130 --> 00:12:57.780
Just as investment requires 
ethics and vision,

00:12:57.780 --> 00:13:00.400
a life requires style.

00:13:00.400 --> 00:13:03.880
In other words, this is 
where we show our stuff.

00:13:04.780 --> 00:13:08.050
After you avoided us and looked 
down on us so many times?

00:13:08.050 --> 00:13:10.460
So you really<i> do</i> sing a different 
tune when Gora-san's involved!

00:13:10.460 --> 00:13:12.460
I knew it, but it's still irritating.

00:13:12.460 --> 00:13:15.480
As people who worked our fingers 
to the bone to become idols...

00:13:15.890 --> 00:13:18.310
Is being an idol really that hard?

00:13:19.270 --> 00:13:20.230
You bet it is!

00:13:21.690 --> 00:13:25.240
If the fun parts don't outweigh the 
hard parts, I think that's wrong!

00:13:25.940 --> 00:13:26.710
Are you stupid?

00:13:26.710 --> 00:13:28.700
That's mere idealism!

00:13:28.700 --> 00:13:29.780
Look at reality!

00:13:30.010 --> 00:13:32.240
I'm having fun in the Defense Club.

00:13:32.400 --> 00:13:33.750
And in the Battle Lovers, too!

00:13:34.020 --> 00:13:37.340
I think it's amazing to 
knuckle down and work hard,

00:13:37.340 --> 00:13:39.710
but won't that eventually 
lead you to a dead end?

00:13:39.950 --> 00:13:44.290
It's wonderful to do stuff for 
some person or some goal, too...

00:13:44.290 --> 00:13:47.680
But in the end, doesn't it come 
down to whether you like it or not?

00:13:48.130 --> 00:13:49.010
You make me sick!

00:13:50.550 --> 00:13:52.120
Losers, stand aside!

00:13:52.120 --> 00:13:54.060
We aim for the top!

00:13:54.510 --> 00:13:55.870
Who are you calling losers?

00:13:55.870 --> 00:13:57.520
I'd like you to amend that statement!

00:13:57.690 --> 00:13:58.400
I don't think so!

00:13:58.710 --> 00:14:01.110
Sure-Kill Thundering Comet!

00:14:02.840 --> 00:14:03.360
Ryuu!

00:14:03.360 --> 00:14:04.030
Io!

00:14:04.220 --> 00:14:08.250
Doing something to be better than 
others is the dumbest thing there is!

00:14:08.250 --> 00:14:10.180
I'd rather have people say 
"he sucks, but I like him"

00:14:10.180 --> 00:14:13.020
or "he's awkward, but I like him."

00:14:13.020 --> 00:14:15.080
If someone told me they liked 
me because I'm the best...

00:14:15.080 --> 00:14:16.120
I'd hate that!

00:14:16.360 --> 00:14:17.790
Stop dreaming!

00:14:17.790 --> 00:14:19.460
Being an idol is a business!

00:14:19.740 --> 00:14:21.420
The business of giving dreams to others!

00:14:21.590 --> 00:14:23.630
But is there love there?!

00:14:24.910 --> 00:14:25.710
No!

00:14:25.710 --> 00:14:26.010
What?!

00:14:28.430 --> 00:14:30.390
A complete repudiation of love?!

00:14:30.680 --> 00:14:33.560
They're still capable of
pushing back against Hakone Yumoto?

00:14:33.760 --> 00:14:36.950
What idols need aren't dreams, but lies!

00:14:36.950 --> 00:14:39.330
You trick people, deceive them, entice them.

00:14:39.330 --> 00:14:40.190
That's what it means...

00:14:41.130 --> 00:14:42.240
...to be an idol!

00:14:45.670 --> 00:14:48.480
Everything we've done has been for Gorar-san!

00:14:48.480 --> 00:14:50.660
All of it for this day!

00:14:50.950 --> 00:14:53.100
We belong to Gorar-san...

00:14:53.100 --> 00:14:55.370
And Gorar-san belongs to us!

00:14:58.080 --> 00:14:59.160
Bro!

00:14:59.160 --> 00:15:00.450
Bro!

00:15:01.630 --> 00:15:03.770
You, who speak only in platitudes...

00:15:03.770 --> 00:15:06.210
...are weaker than us, who 
act in pure self-interest!

00:15:06.590 --> 00:15:08.410
Feeling always triumphs...

00:15:08.410 --> 00:15:09.950
...over reason!

00:15:11.130 --> 00:15:12.300
Bro!

00:15:25.710 --> 00:15:27.100
Big bro?

00:15:28.580 --> 00:15:32.830
Big bro!

00:15:36.980 --> 00:15:37.910
Yumoto?

00:15:38.810 --> 00:15:40.110
Haru! Don't falter!

00:15:40.110 --> 00:15:42.040
I'm not faltering!

00:15:44.220 --> 00:15:46.190
What were you thinking, VEPPer?

00:15:46.750 --> 00:15:48.160
What do you mean?

00:15:48.160 --> 00:15:49.180
If it's a contest of feelings,

00:15:49.180 --> 00:15:51.080
Yumoto's are going to be 
stronger than VEPPer's.

00:15:51.080 --> 00:15:53.060
Overwhelmingly so.

00:15:53.060 --> 00:15:54.680
Talk about a miscalculation...

00:15:56.900 --> 00:16:01.780
No! Bro! Come back to me!

00:16:04.080 --> 00:16:05.220
What we're seeing...

00:16:05.220 --> 00:16:06.910
The souls of the Hakone Yumoto of the present

00:16:06.910 --> 00:16:10.690
and the Hakone Yumoto of the past are 
resonating with each other across space-time?

00:16:10.960 --> 00:16:11.680
Yumoto!

00:16:11.680 --> 00:16:12.430
Calm down!

00:16:12.430 --> 00:16:14.170
He's losing himself to his fear!

00:16:14.170 --> 00:16:15.250
You mean he's out of control?

00:16:15.250 --> 00:16:17.990
Dammit, what are you doing, you idiot?!

00:16:19.350 --> 00:16:22.080
Y-Y-Yumoto-san!

00:16:22.300 --> 00:16:25.150
Big bro! Where are you?!

00:16:25.150 --> 00:16:26.220
H-He's...

00:16:26.220 --> 00:16:27.250
Unbelievable!

00:16:30.700 --> 00:16:32.800
I'm taking back my brother!

00:16:35.140 --> 00:16:36.890
Ultimate...

00:16:36.890 --> 00:16:38.010
Love...

00:16:38.010 --> 00:16:39.040
Attack!

00:16:39.040 --> 00:16:39.450
Yumoto!

00:16:39.450 --> 00:16:39.890
Yumoto!

00:16:39.890 --> 00:16:40.970
Yumoto!

00:16:44.240 --> 00:16:45.100
Stop it, Yumoto!

00:16:45.100 --> 00:16:46.150
You mustn't!

00:16:46.150 --> 00:16:48.020
Don't forget the true nature of love!

00:16:48.020 --> 00:16:48.770
Yumoto!

00:16:48.770 --> 00:16:49.980
What is love?

00:16:51.190 --> 00:16:52.650
Answer us, Yumoto!

00:16:56.870 --> 00:16:57.770
I...

00:16:57.770 --> 00:16:58.920
Stupid Yumoto!

00:16:58.920 --> 00:16:59.750
Really.

00:16:59.750 --> 00:17:02.010
We have such a troublesome kouhai among us.

00:17:02.010 --> 00:17:04.000
Get a grip. I mean it.

00:17:04.310 --> 00:17:06.600
Don't forget, your brother Gora 
isn't the only one in your life.

00:17:06.600 --> 00:17:08.750
You have all of us, too.

00:17:08.750 --> 00:17:10.780
I'm sorry, Senpai.

00:17:11.260 --> 00:17:16.540
I was alone in the dark, 
with the cold wind blowing,

00:17:16.540 --> 00:17:18.950
when I heard your voices...

00:17:18.950 --> 00:17:20.560
I understand now.

00:17:20.800 --> 00:17:22.140
The "Ai" in "Idol"

00:17:22.410 --> 00:17:24.030
is the "Ai" of Love!

00:17:26.240 --> 00:17:27.610
Is he going berserk again?

00:17:27.610 --> 00:17:28.560
No, it's something else!

00:17:39.070 --> 00:17:40.530
Th-This is...

00:17:41.570 --> 00:17:44.040
This is the Ultra More-Better Version!

00:17:44.240 --> 00:17:45.370
Not again!

00:17:46.920 --> 00:17:52.310
To me, idols are people I feel 
better just having around!

00:17:52.310 --> 00:17:55.920
Just knowing they're there 
makes me feel stronger.

00:17:55.920 --> 00:17:58.760
Just like En-chan-senpai and Atsushi-senpai

00:17:58.760 --> 00:18:00.280
and Io-senpai and Ryuu-senpai!

00:18:02.790 --> 00:18:06.120
That's what my brother was to 
you, right, Brothers-senpai?

00:18:06.650 --> 00:18:08.980
And if you're an idol yourself,

00:18:08.980 --> 00:18:12.290
I think you should want to make 
the people around you happy!

00:18:12.290 --> 00:18:13.530
As many people as possible!

00:18:13.760 --> 00:18:14.980
The spiral of love...

00:18:15.190 --> 00:18:16.440
Of loving and being loved...

00:18:16.670 --> 00:18:17.900
It continues onward...

00:18:18.110 --> 00:18:19.240
For eternity!

00:18:19.510 --> 00:18:22.010
That is the "ai" of idols!

00:18:24.790 --> 00:18:28.710
Ultra True Love Attack!

00:18:53.910 --> 00:18:54.970
Yumoto?

00:18:54.970 --> 00:18:56.640
Is something the matter?

00:18:56.640 --> 00:18:58.310
Are you sick to your stomach again?

00:18:58.310 --> 00:19:00.260
No, I'm okay.

00:19:00.660 --> 00:19:01.620
I see.

00:19:02.480 --> 00:19:05.340
I was having a dream.

00:19:05.340 --> 00:19:06.510
What was it?

00:19:06.510 --> 00:19:08.000
Tell me, big bro.

00:19:08.420 --> 00:19:11.490
It was a dream about many 
people I met long ago,

00:19:11.490 --> 00:19:13.460
when I did many things.

00:19:16.220 --> 00:19:17.040
Oh?

00:19:17.040 --> 00:19:18.080
You two...

00:19:19.080 --> 00:19:21.930
Are you the children from Binan Land?

00:19:22.250 --> 00:19:23.350
Gorar?

00:19:23.350 --> 00:19:25.890
How could you tell?

00:19:26.160 --> 00:19:27.420
How?

00:19:27.840 --> 00:19:30.100
You were in my dream, too.

00:19:33.620 --> 00:19:34.270
Why?

00:19:34.270 --> 00:19:38.530
Why do you have to address us 
when we're at our most pathetic?

00:19:39.480 --> 00:19:40.420
Pathetic?

00:19:40.790 --> 00:19:41.710
How?

00:19:41.990 --> 00:19:44.120
You've grown so big and strong.

00:19:46.580 --> 00:19:49.560
You kept your promise to Gorar, didn't you?

00:19:49.960 --> 00:19:50.790
I'm happy.

00:19:54.440 --> 00:19:56.100
What's all this?

00:19:56.100 --> 00:19:57.910
What's wrong, you two?

00:20:01.930 --> 00:20:08.620
<i>VEPPer, the twin stars 
racing through the galaxy!</i>

00:20:08.620 --> 00:20:11.980
<i>Let's illuminate the mysteries 
of the universe...</i>

00:20:11.980 --> 00:20:14.940
<i>On the name of the stars!</i>

00:20:15.220 --> 00:20:17.650
Thanks for listening to us
all the way to the end!

00:20:17.650 --> 00:20:22.400
We're so happy to know that 
our songs can help you!

00:20:22.720 --> 00:20:26.720
To be honest, VEPPer has been through a lot, 
and we've had a lot of setbacks lately.

00:20:26.720 --> 00:20:30.250
But now we understand what it is
that we really love to do!

00:20:30.550 --> 00:20:33.430
We're grateful to the 
people who taught us that.

00:20:33.430 --> 00:20:36.420
And we love you, Beppu Apes!

00:20:43.060 --> 00:20:43.590
So?

00:20:43.900 --> 00:20:45.170
So what?

00:20:45.170 --> 00:20:47.000
Well, any stories?

00:20:47.000 --> 00:20:47.930
No.

00:20:48.180 --> 00:20:49.880
Oh, come on.

00:20:49.880 --> 00:20:52.020
You had fun, right?

00:20:52.020 --> 00:20:53.140
Did we?

00:20:53.140 --> 00:20:54.410
It was pretty standard.

00:20:54.410 --> 00:20:56.640
Well, there was that one interesting thing.

00:20:56.640 --> 00:20:57.940
Jellied eels.

00:20:58.100 --> 00:20:58.960
Whatted whats?

00:20:58.960 --> 00:21:00.380
It's a local dish.

00:21:00.380 --> 00:21:02.280
Eel should be done kabayaki style!

00:21:02.280 --> 00:21:04.630
I don't know why you expect me to defend it.

00:21:04.630 --> 00:21:06.310
Boy, do you suck.

00:21:06.930 --> 00:21:08.520
Did they have hot baths?

00:21:08.520 --> 00:21:10.740
No, just shower booths.

00:21:10.740 --> 00:21:14.480
They looked a bit like toilets, 
all lined up in a row.

00:21:14.880 --> 00:21:16.710
See? That's interesting.

00:21:16.710 --> 00:21:18.170
Tell us more stuff like that.

00:21:18.430 --> 00:21:21.250
But at the end of the day, 
soaking in a hot bath is the best.

00:21:21.600 --> 00:21:23.770
There goes Yumoto, jumping to philosophy.

00:21:23.770 --> 00:21:26.430
But I think I understand what he means.

00:21:26.640 --> 00:21:31.060
It's the bath that makes the Earth 
Defense Club what it is, right?

00:21:31.260 --> 00:21:32.270
Yeah!

00:21:32.270 --> 00:21:33.270
And...

00:21:34.450 --> 00:21:36.770
We have new members, too!

00:21:36.770 --> 00:21:37.490
Yeah...

00:21:37.860 --> 00:21:40.130
And now we're all together!

00:21:40.130 --> 00:21:40.840
But...

00:21:40.840 --> 00:21:42.830
I feel like someone's missing.

00:21:42.830 --> 00:21:44.150
Erk!

00:21:44.150 --> 00:21:45.920
Gora-san's chopping wood, right?

00:21:45.920 --> 00:21:49.930
Zundar and Dadacha went 
back to space together...

00:21:49.930 --> 00:21:50.790
So who could it be?

00:21:50.790 --> 00:21:52.080
Good question...

00:23:54.910 --> 00:23:58.790
<b>Important news after the break!</b>

00:23:58.790 --> 00:24:01.710
<b><Important News></b>

00:24:01.710 --> 00:24:08.670
<b>Mr. Tawarayama was once again brought back to life thanks
 to the "life" brought to Earth by one of Wombat's people.
 Thank goodness.</b>

00:24:08.670 --> 00:24:10.670
<b></b>
